const guide=[['Gus × Seerr','Design proposal · 20 October 2026\nApp source checkpoint: d715c05\nFictional artwork, titles, people and addresses. No app code changes.\n\nThe integration script places these screens on the Discover Proposal page of each matching 05 Discover.fig file. This specifies a proposed expanded native client, not an already implemented release.'],['Design direction','Artwork first. Native navigation. Clear request outcomes.\n\nUse semantic Apple surfaces and SF Pro. Reserve Winter Chill colors for accents and artwork. Native materials/chrome are approximations here. Poster content is cinematic; toolbars, controls, sheets and sidebars belong to each platform. Avoid a miniature Seerr website.'],['Scope & implementation boundary','Retain: connect/hide, separate server/sign-in, catalog/search, requests, seasons, manager decisions, per-device sessions and Jellyfin provider-ID matching.\n\nExpand: rich shelves/grid, cast/crew/recommendations, advanced request choices, reports/comments, blocklist, server-backed notification preferences. See DISCOVER.md for API and permission gates.\n\nNo native push promise. No generic local watchlist masquerading as Seerr sync. Full infrastructure settings and service secrets remain in the Seerr web UI. Watch has no Discover.'],['Interactions','Layer names [go:state] are interaction annotations. The shared Preview.html provides synthetic navigation in Discover proposal mode. OpenPencil screen-to-screen reactions are not wired.\n\nTab order and root destination visibility remain user-configurable. Phone artboards show a user-customized direct Discover tab. Default ordering remains governed by Gus navigation preferences.'],['Recovery & safety','Server-confirmed mutations only. Refresh uncertain results before retrying. Separate approval status from media availability. No invented download percentages, ETAs, event history or local approval success. Permission and quota changes refresh eligibility.\n\nRestricted titles disappear and selections clear. Available does not imply accessible in this Jellyfin account. Play appears only after accessible exact provider-ID matching.'],['Platform behavior','iPhone: NavigationStack, native sheets/forms, searchable, TabView. iPad: adaptive split layout; collapse at compact width. Mac: sidebar/toolbar, keyboard focus, native search field, inspector, context menus. Narrow Mac replaces inspector with detail navigation. TV: large type and remote focus; detail remains readable from the couch. Vision: native window/sidebar/ornaments and 60-point interaction targets; flat diagrams do not certify depth or gaze.'],['Review & acceptance','Editable native text/vector layers, reusable components and auto-layout. Light/dark key flows plus explicit adaptive layouts, not every state in every appearance.\n\nReferences/QA/Discover holds integrated validation and review images. Final app work still needs native material, Dynamic Type, VoiceOver, focus/keyboard/remote/gaze, live Seerr acceptance and physical-device review. Artwork is original synthetic placeholder content, not actual catalog art.']];
for(const [i,[title,body]]of guide.entries())await core.renderJSX(g,col(title,800,text(title,32,c.text,700)+text(body,18,c.secondary),20,'p={32} bg="#1D2023" rounded={20}'),{parentId:pages[5].id,x:80+(i%2)*900,y:80+Math.floor(i/2)*520});
